2.1.8 Transition Zone Modelling
Transition zone models aim to improve the accuracy of simulations in the transition region
(Re ≅ 5 × 105), where the flow is neither fully turbulent nor laminar. These models are most
useful for flow that transitions at a point further from the ends of a body. For example, flow at
Mach 2 will enter the transition zone after ~11 mm. In this case, the flow will become turbulent
so quickly that it becomes unnecessary to accurately model the transition zone, as the flow will
be turbulent for over 99% of a 5 m long rocket. Therefore, for high-speed external flows,
transition zone models are not required.
