The dynamic pressure is a non-negative quantity, as fluid density and velocity are non-negative
quantities. At take-off, the rocket velocity is at zero, so according to Equation 2.38, the dynamic
pressure is zero. Once the rocket reaches space, the fluid density is zero, so according to
Equation 2.38, the dynamic pressure is zero. Therefore, there exists a point in the rocket flight
where there is a maximum dynamic pressure. This point is known as ‘max q’.
Max q is the limiting factor for the structural design of the rocket, because the maximum
mechanical stress occurs at max q. Determining max q and the maximum stress on the rocket
is crucial for designing its structure. If the maximum stress is under-predicted, then the rocket
could undergo catastrophic failure during flight. If the maximum stress is over-predicted, then
