large. The large average value could be due to the hexcore section of the mesh. Due to
the definition of hexcore, when a small hexahedral element transitions to a larger
hexahedral element, the side length doubles, and the volume increases by a factor of 8.
Star-CCM+ mesh:
• The average and minimum aspect ratios were 0.9385 and 0.01175 respectively. No
guidelines were provided by Star-CCM+ for the cell aspect ratio, except that values
closer to 1 are preferred, which was achieved in this mesh.


