Figure 56. Wake Meshing Areas
Free stream: The free stream area is the coarsest as there is usually no change in flow properties
between adjacent cells, so small cells are not required. This is not the case when there is shock
wave formation, as the shock waves propagate into the free stream and there are large changes
in flow properties across the shock waves. Shock wave refinement was dealt with in the following manner. As part of the general mesh refinement, the free stream was refined, and
therefore the shock waves were refined. At supersonic speeds, convergence was observed, as
shown in the Chapter 5.1. This showed that a standard mesh refinement can be used to account
for shock waves in the free stream.
