coefficient rapidly increases is called drag divergence. For the region up until drag divergence,
the skin friction drag, pressure drag, and total drag increase with Mach number at similar rates
to the dynamic pressure. This is shown by the relatively constant Cd values up to drag
divergence. At the drag divergence, there is shock wave formation, which greatly increases
wave drag (a type of pressure drag). The pressure drag increases at much higher rates compared
to the dynamic pressure, up until a peak Cd is reached. After the peak Cd, the dynamic pressure
increases at slightly higher rates than the pressure drag, shown by slowly decreasing Cd values.
The rate that the skin friction coefficient changes with Mach number stays relatively constant
as it is not affected by the onset of wave drag.
